00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:33.990
<b>~But I Understand~」</b>

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:33.990
<b>~But I Understand~」</b>

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:36.950
Good morning!

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:37.910
Good morning.

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:42.700
Here you are!

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:43.910
Thank you.

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:05.220
All right.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:25.040
What is it, Mikado-sensei?

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:26.540
You keep sighing.

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:27.200
Eh?

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.420
You shouldn't make such a meek-looking face!

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:31.920
Smile! Smile!

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.130
You're always so energetic, Oshizu-chan.

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:41.550
Honekawa-sensei is returning to teach, right?

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:43.850
Oh, that's right!

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:47.020
It seems he recovered from his back pain with the invention he got from Lala-san.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:47.930
I'm so glad.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:53.440
Tear has been removed from her temporary assistant position because of it, though.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:58.820
Now she'll become homeroom teacher for class 1-B in place of Ogawa-sensei.

00:02:58.820 --> 00:02:59.820
Class B?

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.070
Is that the one with Momo-san, Yami-san and the others?

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:06.540
But Yami-chan is still awkward around Tear, right?

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:10.540
I was thinking this could be a chance for something to happen.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:21.220
I'm also concerned if it will go well with Mea-san, who says she hates Tear.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:26.350
That's true...

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:28.020
Hm?

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:30.350
Oh, you're going to read that?

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:38.690
Oh, Tearju-sensei.

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:41.740
Honekawa-sensei, how are you feeling?

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:45.240
Thanks to you, I was able to take it easy and recuperate.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:48.490
I'm sorry it took so long.

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:49.620
It's no problem.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:54.130
Thanks to Lala-san, it looks like I'll be able to work hard for a while.

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:01.880
Oh my, are you nervous?

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:03.930
Well... yes.

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:05.850
You should relax.

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:09.010
Your nervousness will be conveyed to the students.

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:10.180
Come on, smile.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:12.940
Yes.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.810
Just like that.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.360
Thank you.

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:23.110
I'll be going now.

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:25.570
I need to be on my way.

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:30.950
Is he really okay?

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:36.960
That's right.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:38.460
A smile, a smile.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:44.340
Oh, my.

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:52.140
From now on, I'll be your homeroom teacher.

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:54.270
Please treat me well, everyone.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:55.940
Oh! Awesome!

00:04:55.940 --> 00:04:57.270
I wonder how this came to be.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:58.020
Nice!

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:28.590
Eh?

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:32.220
Tearju-sensei became your homeroom teacher?

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:32.930
Yes.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:35.270
What about Yami?

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:41.270
Just a while ago I suggested for her to go to class, but...

00:05:41.730 --> 00:05:44.860
Why are you telling me this now, Princess Momo?

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:48.110
It has nothing to do with me.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:50.830
That's what she said to me.

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:52.120
I see.

00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:58.870
Those two have finally been reunited, so it would be a shame for things to remain awkward between them.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:04.710
I was looking forward to seeing her in a school uniform.

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:07.550
Yeah, it would.

00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:08.840
Okay!

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:11.390
I'll try talking to Yami after school.

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:12.220
Yes.

00:06:15.180 --> 00:06:16.230
No way!

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:17.850
I'm telling you, it's true!

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:19.850
I don't believe it!

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:26.610
Goodbye, Tear-sensei.

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:28.030
Goodbye.

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:29.860
Ah...

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:48.220
See you tomorrow, Mikan!

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:49.840
Bye!

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:52.600
Huh?

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:56.850
What is it?

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:59.060
It's unusual for you to come meet me.

00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:00.980
I just felt like it.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:02.350
Hmm...

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:04.730
What should we do today?

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:16.290
m 0 0 l 173 0 173 35 0 35

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:16.290
Sainan Library

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:23.170
Ugh... this is difficult.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:26.710
I'm surprised you can understand this, Yami-san.

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:28.170
Is it interesting?

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:29.720
It is interesting.

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:33.260
Like what?

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:38.180
Books teach a lot to someone who knows nothing, like myself.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:41.480
Earth's history. Science. Nature.

00:07:42.060 --> 00:07:43.440
People's hearts.

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:48.690
You should read a lot of books too, Mikan.

00:07:50.190 --> 00:07:52.360
I think I'll choose something a little less difficult.

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:08.300
You haven't changed from the past at all, Yami-san.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:09.550
What do you mean?

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:16.720
Tearju-san said you loved having books read to you when you were little.

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:21.140
She said you would ask her to read a number of books before bed, so it was difficult.

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:26.270
But also that it was very fun.

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:30.480
Oh... What is it?

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:31.280
Nothing.

00:08:32.360 --> 00:08:34.990
What else did you talk about with Tear?

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:37.070
Hm? Various things.

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:40.540
She told me a lot about when you were a child.

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:43.290
Is that so?

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:45.250
Speaking of which, Yami-san...

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:48.420
Ever since Tearju-san came, you haven't attended class, right?

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:50.420
Well, yes...

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:51.300
Why?

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:54.970
You should show her how you look in your school uniform.

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:01.970
You are aware of the fact that you are something that doesn't belong here.

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:13.030
Come again!

00:09:13.030 --> 00:09:15.070
She's not here either, huh?

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:17.910
Where else would Yami go...?

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:23.000
Senpai!

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:23.000
Ah!

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:24.200
Mea!

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:27.000
Seeing you alone is so unusual, Senpai!

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.210
Let's go play!

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:31.130
I'm sorry, but I'm busy right now.

00:09:31.130 --> 00:09:32.340
What's with that!

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:33.800
You played with Master!

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:40.220
I heard that Master washed your body in the bath.

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:43.060
I'm really interested in that.

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:44.640
No, that was-

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:55.070
What's going on?!

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:57.320
Welcome to the dream world!

00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:59.280
Why are we in a bath?!

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:05.250
This is a dream I made using your memories as a base, Senpai.

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:12.670
Eh...

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:15.960
So you did something like this with Master?

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:17.720
How wonderful!

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:22.680
Isn't it, Senpai?

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:35.690
It seems like Master has really taken a liking to you.

00:10:39.490 --> 00:10:42.620
But it's a little complicating for me...

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:53.130
Because it'll be hard for me to play with you like this if you belong to Master.

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:59.010
Mea! S-Stop! M-Mea...{he keeps stammering like this after Mea speaks}

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:58.420
Hm? You want me to stop?

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:00.260
Nope!

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:03.260
I really like playing this way!

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:06.220
It's slippery and feels good!

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:11.270
Why don't we try it for real next time, Senpai?

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:20.150
No, I, I... Yami! Yami!

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:22.530
Yami-oneechan?

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:25.410
What about Yami-oneechan?

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:34.250
So that's what you meant.

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:36.380
Mea...

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:40.670
Mea, what do you think?

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:41.550
About what?

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:48.270
Do you think it would be good if Yami and Tearju-sensei made up?

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:50.140
Not particularly.

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:52.640
I don't have much interest in Tearju.

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:58.730
I would like for you to think about them more, Mea.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:00.150
Me? Why?

00:12:00.940 --> 00:12:07.160
Because Tearju-sensei said you were like her little sister to her, Mea.

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:13.000
You and Yami are both dear family to Sensei.

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:15.960
So I want you to see each other.

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:21.880
If not, I don't think you can ever make amends with each other.

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:22.760
I'm going home.

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:23.970
Mea!

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:27.970
I wonder if I said something I shouldn't have.

00:12:32.310 --> 00:12:33.850
Well then, I'll be going.

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:37.610
Is something the matter?

00:12:38.480 --> 00:12:39.820
Are you okay?

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:41.280
What do you mean?

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:47.700
I can't stop worrying about it.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:50.290
Yami-san, come over for dinner tonight.

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:50.870
Eh?

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:52.160
Yeah, let's do that.

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:53.330
Come on.

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:57.420
No, I'll pass for today.

00:12:58.000 --> 00:12:59.000
See you.

00:13:14.480 --> 00:13:15.850
What an idiot...

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:30.950
Hey, I said wait!

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:32.950
Hey! Wai-

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:40.170
m 0 0 l 437 0 437 95 0 95

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:40.170
Sainan Library

00:13:57.350 --> 00:14:01.020
I'm surprised you knew I was here, Yuuki Rito.

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:06.070
I heard from Mikan that you've been coming here often recently.

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:07.740
Is that so?

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:10.490
So? What did you come to do?

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:13.740
Uh, uhm, uhh...

00:14:21.170 --> 00:14:22.240
What is it?

00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:27.090
Uh, I thought maybe I'd read something, too.

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:47.440
Yuuki Rito.

00:14:47.440 --> 00:14:49.950
You should study more as well.

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:52.990
Y-Yeah, I should...

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:56.330
It seems you only think about perverted things,

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:58.460
so you should replace your brain.

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:01.670
I'm not only thinking about things like that!

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:06.210
Or perhaps... I should replace it for you?

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:07.960
Ah... No, that's fine.

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:08.920
I'm sorry.

